# Objective

Detect command-line creation of Windows scheduled tasks that may represent persistence or suspicious execution activity.

DET-004 focuses on the behavioral combination:

```text
schtasks.exe
      +
/create
```

rather than alerting on all scheduled-task activity.

Scheduled tasks are widely used by legitimate Windows software and administrators.

DET-004 therefore represents an investigation signal rather than proof of malicious activity.

---

# Data Requirements

DET-004 requires endpoint telemetry containing scheduled-task command-line activity.

Observable data should provide visibility into:

```text
schtasks.exe
/create
task name
task action
host
timestamp
```

Additional useful context may include:

```text
User
Parent Process
Command Line
Process
Task XML
Security Context
```

