# Detection Logic Explained

```text
Endpoint Telemetry
       |
       v
schtasks.exe?
   /       \
 NO        YES
 |          |
 v          v
Ignore    /create?
          /    \
         NO    YES
         |      |
         v      v
      Ignore  DET-004
```

This separates task creation from ordinary task enumeration.

---

# Controlled Validation

A harmless scheduled task was created:

```cmd
schtasks /create /tn "Sprint22-DET004-Positive" /tr "cmd.exe /c echo DET004 Positive >> C:\Windows\Temp\DET004.txt" /sc once /st 23:59 /f
```

The task simply referenced a local command that writes benign text.

No harmful persistence payload was used.

---

# Positive Validation

The controlled task creation was located in Splunk.

Validation search:

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" "Sprint22-DET004-Positive"
```

The activity contained the observable scheduled-task creation behavior required by DET-004.

Result:

```text
DET-004 TRIGGERED
```

**Positive Test:** PASS

---

# Negative Validation

Normal task enumeration was performed:

```cmd
schtasks /query
```

and:

```powershell
Get-ScheduledTask | Select-Object -First 5
```

The activity did not contain `/create`.

Result:

```text
DET-004 NOT TRIGGERED
```

**Negative Test:** PASS

