# Task Action Analysis

The task action is one of the most important investigative components.

Examples requiring additional scrutiny could include tasks launching:

```text
powershell.exe
cmd.exe
scripts
unknown executables
executables from unusual locations
```

These are not inherently malicious.

They provide context for additional investigation.

---

# Execution Context

Analysts should determine whether the task executes as:

```text
Current User
Administrator
SYSTEM
Service Account
Other Account
```

Privileged execution can increase the impact of suspicious scheduled-task activity.

---

